## Threats considered (import expand)

### T1 — Path traversal via import name

**Mitigated** for `..`, abs `/`, `~`, `\`. Nested `..` and `//` covered.

### T2 — Symlink / relative outside project (no `..` in name)

**Residual MED:** `import "out_link.oo"` where `out_link.oo` → absolute
outside file **loads and checks OK**. Relative names without `..` follow FS
symlinks / any readable path under `path_join(dir, imp)`. No realpath /
O_NOFOLLOW on import load (contrast FFI open policy). Not classic `..`
escape; still arbitrary-read-as-source if attacker plants a symlink in the
project tree.

### T3 — Std probe CWD coupling

**Residual LOW:** host-relative `../std` … `../../../std` can resolve std
from unexpected CWD. Not home-absolute; fail-closed if not found.

### T4 — Residual shell concat (`oodac_concat.sh`)

**Residual MED (non-product default):** script `abspath` accepts leading `/`
import names; **no** `reject_bad_import_name` parity. Product check/emit
default uses in-tree `load_import`. Documented residual for
`EMIT_CONCAT=1` / pure_build script path — do not treat as sealed product
import ZT.

### T5 — Empty import line

`import "";` → `parse_import_line` returns empty (not-import); body tokens
kept; check may OK. **Residual LOW** (no file load). Empty branch in
`reject_bad_import_name` is effectively dead for this parse surface.

### T6 — NUL import name

Source + binary have explicit NUL reject; live C string path may truncate
at NUL → "not found" fail-closed without NUL-specific message. **Residual LOW**.

### T7 — Partial emit after load fail

`emit-c` prints preamble then load reject (rc=1). **Residual LOW** honesty
(partial stdout); exit remains non-zero.

### T8 — Issue #9 line/path attribution

Type errors in imports report **expanded-stream** LINE:COL. Usability /
agent triage residual — **not** fail-open of the type gate itself.

### T9 — H6 size gates

Per-file 64KiB at CLI load (`main.oo`); expanded 1MiB in `run_check_core`.
DoS/cost residual; fail-closed when exceeded.

